{"title":"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 5b","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2019 CEMC Euclid Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the system of equations: \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c43a629e93b14aab4dee302b3f9acca475e552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d=2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" /></center> \n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc9f9909b3d8a95555c84efe49910182edf878c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{c}{d}=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"50\" height=\"34\" /></center>\n<p>Determine the number of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/f/94f992d81eb41a2b9aae683d440c0d0f9495005f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\geq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> for which there is at least one pair of integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/e/79e31171b9eaf222673b566ed3cf773e0f0b532c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(c,d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> that is a solution to the system.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5b&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the second equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/7/a5775d8641487b2ca7ffae9e305cfd37e4f10269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = dk$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Plugging this into the first equation, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1921d942953df2bcbf83d5e008e8c34f873bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$dk + d = 2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421712bb77bedef778ccd80d252d1d6420fd5062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(k + 1) = 2000 = 2^{4} \\times 5^{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>From the prime factorization, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f1ffc8a6829f25b0b0366087a70dfd4e06fef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32b1766d0407b2a0907c45473283aeda0dd5e188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4 + 1)(3 + 1) = 5 \\times 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"218\" height=\"20\" /> positive factors. We could have also listed all of the factors to get this:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/a/fea5fcc6d66685ee21f722efcd228eb44d38f262.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448b3c8f2596d1b93b4b3ef199f8b3241ced9da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/9/e8924412a12becf7905729885a46e3e351ec5a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/9/a39b14023c98c943554d150561aacc188c4ce26d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$500$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f1ffc8a6829f25b0b0366087a70dfd4e06fef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/99811de702457c19abc7e3ab6eebab9927d09393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1 \\geq 0 + 1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" /> from the inequality given in the first problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/8/e18453e31b8b9f4f7722777b72a0eff030a17d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> can be any positive integer as long as it is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f1ffc8a6829f25b0b0366087a70dfd4e06fef6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8bf3c869ee37d06e7ee0ec276b06aa2f02027c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> possible values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018010947\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 125/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 78/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6165/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.866      1 2019_CEMC_Euclid_Problems/Problem_5\n100.00%    5.866      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35926:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018010947 and revision id 279855. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}